    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`):\n\n- **Added an `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 a `Logger` obtained via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, the dedicated logger name the spec and `AuditLogCapture` test helper expect.\n- **Emitted the audit line after a successful save** in `addOwner`, right after `saveOwner(owner)` so the owner has its generated id, `customerCode` and resolved `registrationDate`:\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n```\n\nThe line carries all three required values (owner id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`). The new `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
